ch is split into eight 8-bit segments. Each segment passes through a corresponding substitution box S sub 1 through S sub 8. The output\s are recombined into a second 64-bit intermediate value. A permutation step rearranges the bits to produce the final 64-bit output.␀)/K 0/P 20969 0 R/Pg 3845 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj21162 0 obj<</BBox 21163 0 R/Height 241.36/O/Layout/Width 214.691>>endobj21163 0 obj[112.357 355.693 327.048 597.053]endobj21164 0 obj<</A 21165 0 R/Alt(Three feedback shift registers labeled A, B, and C are connected in a looped structure. Each register contains multiple stages. Selected outputs from each register are used in AND operations, and the results are input to X OR gates which feed into the oth\er registers. The output is derived from a combination of values from all three registers, forming a coupled, nonlinear system.␀)/K 0/P 20969 0 R/Pg 3720 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj21165 0 obj<</BBox 21166 0 R/Height 179.98/O/Layout/Width 279.259>>endobj21166 0 obj[81.639 413.997 360.898 593.977]endobj21167 0 obj<</A 21168 0 R/Alt(Four registers labeled S sub 3 through S sub 0 are connected in series. The output of S sub 3 and S sub 2 are input to an X OR gate, and the result is fed back into the register chain, forming a linear-feedback shift register.␀)/K 0/P 20969 0 R/Pg 3675 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj21168 0 obj<</BBox 21169 0 R/Height 68.1656/O/Layout/Width 173.802>>endobj21169 0 obj[132.515 407.838 306.317 476.003]endobj21170 0 obj<</A 21171 0 R/Alt(A Merkle tree is constructed from eight hashed values H of x sub 1 through H of x sub 8. Each pair of hash values is combined to compute a parent node, proceeding up the tree through h sub 1 to 2, h sub 3 to 4, h sub 5 to 6, and h sub 7 to 8. These are th\en combined to compute h sub 1 to 4 and h sub 5 to 8, and finally merged to produce the root hash h sub 1 to 8.␀)/K 0/P 20969 0 R/Pg 3492 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>endobj21171 0 obj<</BBox 21172 0 R/Height 143.982/O/Layout/Width 2